README.OSK -- what was changed to build CMDS/screen and REBUILT/screen_nocioscandir.c: `filecnt' is now set to 0.  The original declares it`register int filecnt;' and never initialises it, then stores each fileit accepts at dirlist[filecnt++] -- so the first store went wherever theregister happened to point.  Under os9exec that was a bus error at thefirst file accepted from $HOME/.SCREENS (measured 2026-09-22, in both thisbuild and the archive's own); on the machine it was written on theregister evidently held something harmless.  One line; nothing else ischanged.2026-09-26: CMDS/screen is now this source built the same way, withits module named `screen'.  The archive's own cio build it replacedstopped with that bus error at the first file, which is the only thingthe program is for.  Measured: with $HOME/.SCREENS/hi holding a commandline, the new build runs it; the old one took the bus error.(tools/datatests/PA.cases.)